    "field": "Physical oceanography",
    "problem": "Understanding the mechanisms driving decadal-scale regional sea-level variability is challenging because the specific roles of, and interplay between, ocean circulation changes and atmospheric wind forcing in the North Atlantic are not fully resolved, particularly for the recent satellite altimetry era.",
    "method": "This study analyzes decadal sea-level trends by correlating satellite altimetry, hydrographic data, and atmospheric reanalysis during distinct warming (1993\u20132004) and cooling (2005\u20132016) periods to identify links between sea level, ocean circulation, and wind forcing in the North Atlantic.",
    "task": "The task is to investigate decadal sea-level trends in the North Atlantic during the altimetry era and identify the associated changes in ocean circulation and wind patterns that drive the observed variability.",
